Ladybird’s exception logger can read an accessor when JavaScript
is running. For an embedder throw without a running context it
consults the stored property. Other engines’ exception-reporting
interfaces differ. V8’s MessageHandler::ReportMessage()
uses NoSideEffectsToString() for internal errors.
SpiderMonkey’s ErrorReportBuilder::init() has a side-effect-free
reporting mode. WebKit’s retrieveErrorMessageWithoutName() reads
DOMException’s native message directly.

The diagnostic flag and its embedder entry point are specific to
Ladybird. The native regression exercises logging both with a running
context and after the embedder pops it.
